{title: 143 - Silent Night, Holy Night}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Jesus Christ}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Bb]Silent night, holy night;
[F7]All is calm, [Bb]all is bright
[Eb]Round yon virgin [Bb]mother and Child,
[Eb]Holy Infant so [Bb]tender and mild,
[F7]Sleep in heavenly [Bb]peace,
Sleep in [F7]heavenly [Bb]peace.

Verse 2:
[Bb]Silent night! holy night!
[F7]Shepherds quake [Bb]at the sight,
[Eb]glories stream [Bb]from heaven afar,
[Eb]heavenly hosts [Bb]sing Alleluia;
[F7]Christ, the [Bb]Savior is born,
[F7]Christ, the [Bb]Savior is born.

Verse 3:
[Bb]Silent night! holy night!
[F7]Son of God, [Bb]love's pure light,
[Eb]Radiant beams from [Bb]Thy holy face,
[Eb]with the dawn [Bb]of redeeming grace,
[F7]Jesus, Lord, [Bb]at Thy birth,
[F7]Jesus, Lord, [Bb]at Thy birth.
